# Netlify's Neon DB migration checker hashes these files and compares against what was
# recorded as "applied" from the original Linux CI build (LF line endings). Windows'
# core.autocrlf=true checks them out as CRLF locally, which hash-mismatches and fails
# `netlify deploy` (CLI) with "migration ... has been modified after being applied" —
# even though the tracked content never actually changed. Force LF regardless of the
# checkout machine's autocrlf setting so local CLI deploys hash-match CI exactly.
netlify/database/migrations/** text eol=lf
